nd corrections. Voker takes these and uses LLMs and hierarchical text classification to create dynamic categories that give higher level insights so you don’t have to read individual conversations to know what are the main usage patterns across your users.<p>The most common substitute solution we’ve seen is uploading obs logs to Claude or ChatGPT and asking for summary insights. There are a few problems with this - mainly that LLMs aren’t good at math or data science, so you don’t get accurate or consistent statistics. Its highly likely that the LLM overfits to some insights and underfits to others. The LLM isn’t programmatically reading and classifying each individual session or interaction. This is why we don’t use LLMs for any of our core data engineering (processing events, calculating statistics) so the analytics we produce are consistent, reproducible, and accurate.\\nWe have a publicly available, lightweight SDK that wraps LLM calls to OpenAI, Anthropic and Gemini in Python and Typescript. Voker handles the data engineering to turn raw data into usable analytics primitives and higher level insights. \\nFree tier: 2,000 events / mo, requires email signup. Paid plans start at $80/mo with a 30 day free trial.<p>We\'d love to hear how you\'re currently detecting trends, and if you try Voker, tell us what part of our analysis is valuable, and what still feels missing. Thanks for reading, and we’re looking forward to your thoughts in the comments!</p>\\n<hr />\\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\\\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48109962\\\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48109962</a></p>\\n<p>Points: 44</p>\\n<p># Comments: 19</p>\", \"comments\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48109962\", \"published\": \"Tue, 12 May 2026 15:45:20 +0000\", \"guidislink\": false, \"title_detail\": {\"base\": \"https://hnrss.org/frontpage\", \"type\": \"text/plain\", \"value\": \"Launch HN: Voker (YC S24) – Analytics for AI Agents\", \"language\": null}, \"author_detail\": {\"name\": \"ttpost\"}, \"summary_detail\": {\"base\": \"https://hnrss.org/frontpage\", \"type\": \"text/html\", \"value\": \"<p>Hey HN, we\'re Alex and Tyler, co-founders of Voker.ai (<a href=\\\"https://voker.ai/\\\">https://voker.ai/</a>), an agent analytics platform for AI product teams. Voker gives full visibility into what users are asking of your agents, and whether your agents are delivering, without having to dig through logs. Our main product is a lightweight SDK that is LLM stack agnostic and purpose-built for agent products. (<a href=\\\"https://app.voker.ai/docs\\\">https://app.voker.ai/docs</a>)<p>Agent Engineers and AI product teams don’t have the right level of visibility into agent performance in production, which results in bad user experiences, churn, and hundreds of hours wasted with spot checks to find and debug issues with agent configurations.<p>Demo: <a href=\\\"https://www.tella.tv/video/vid_cmoukcsk1000i07jgb4j65u67/view\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">https://www.tella.tv/video/vid_cmoukcsk1000i07jgb4j65u67/vie...</a><p>We recently conducted a survey of YC Founders and 90%+ of respondents said that the only way they know if their Agents are failing users in production is by hearing complaints from customers. They push a prompt change hoping that it fixes the problem and doesn’t break something somewhere else, and the cycle repeats.<p>We saw tons of observability and evals products popping up to try to address these problems, but we still felt like something was missing in the agent monitoring stack. Obs is good for individual trace debugging but is only accessible to engineers. Evals are good for testing known issues, but don\'t give insights into trends that teams don’t expect, so engineers are always playing catch up. Traditional product analytics tools do a good job tracking clicks and pageviews across your product surface but weren’t built ground up for agent products. Knowing what users want out of agents, and whether the agent delivered requires specific conversational intelligence / unstructured data processing techniques.<p>We came up with the agent analytics primitives of Intents, Corrections, and Resolutions to describe something pretty much all conversational agents had in common: a user will always come to an agent with an intent, the user might have to correct this agent on the way to getting their intent resolved, and hopefully every intent a user has is eventually resolved by the agent.\\nVoker processes LLM calls by automatically annotating individual conversations and picking out user intent and corrections. Voker takes these and uses LLMs and hierarchical text classification to create dynamic categories that give higher level insights so you don’t have to read individual conversations to know what are the main usage patterns across your users.<p>The most common substitute solution we’ve seen is uploading obs logs to Claude or ChatGPT and asking for summary insights. There are a few problems with this - mainly that LLMs aren’t good at math or data science, so you don’t get accurate or consistent statistics. Its highly likely that the LLM overfits to some insights and underfits to others. The LLM isn’t programmatically reading and classifying each individual session or interaction. This is why we don’t use LLMs for any of our core data engineering (processing events, calculating statistics) so the analytics we produce are consistent, reproducible, and accurate.\\nWe have a publicly available, lightweight SDK that wraps LLM calls to OpenAI, Anthropic and Gemini in Python and Typescript. Voker handles the data engineering to turn raw data into usable analytics primitives and higher level insights. \\nFree tier: 2,000 events / mo, requires email signup. Paid plans start at $80/mo with a 30 day free trial.<p>We\'d love to hear how you\'re currently detecting trends, and if you try Voker, tell us what part of our analysis is valuable, and what still feels missing. Thanks for reading, and we’re looking forward to your thoughts in the comments!</p>\\n<hr />\\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\\\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48109962\\\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48109962</a></p>\\n<p>Points: 44</p>\\n<p># Comments: 19</p>\", \"language\": null}, \"published_parsed\": [2026, 5, 12, 15, 45, 20, 1, 132, 0]}, \"published_at\": \"2026-05-12 15:45:20\", \"ai_json_output\": \"\"}', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-13 12:08:41');
INSERT INTO `news_detail` VALUES (117, 3842, 6, '科技与数字服务', 'AnySearch 正式发布：为 AI Agent 构建的下一代搜索基础设施，重构搜索底层逻辑', '', '随着 AI Agent 从实验性工具加速进入生产系统，一个新的基础设施问题逐渐显露：当下主流的搜索工具，几乎都是为“人”设计的，而非为“AI”服务。 近日，一款AI搜索产品AnySearch正式发布，并在海外AI开发者圈引发关注。该产品专为AI Agent、企业AI系统设计，旨在为AI Agent提供统一、高质量、结构化的信息搜索层能力。 ...', 'https://www.oschina.net/news/439927', 0, '', '{\"summary\": \"本文为布局出海AI领域的企业开发者介绍了一款新型AI搜索基础设施工具，具备参考价值\", \"abstract\": \"随着AI Agent从实验性工具加速进入生产系统，适配AI需求的搜索基础设施缺口逐渐显现。当前主流搜索工具均面向人类设计，无法满足AI系统的搜索需求。近日，专为AI Agent和企业AI系统打造的AnySearch正式发布。该产品定位下一代搜索基础设施，可提供统一高质量结构化搜索能力，目前已在海外AI开发者圈引发关注\", \"keywords\": [\"AnySearch\", \"AI Agent\", \"搜索基础设施\", \"AI出海\", \"结构化搜索\", \"海外开发者\"], \"policy_risk\": {\"market_risk\": \"未提及\", \"policy_compliance\": \"未提及\"}, \"topic_cluster\": \"AI产品出海\", \"industry_category\": \"科技与数字服务\"}', '', '{\"url\": \"https://www.oschina.net/news/439927\", \"title\": \"AnySearch 正式发布：为 AI Agent 构建的下一代搜索基础设施，重构搜索底层逻辑\", \"source\": \"https://www.oschina.net/news/rss\", \"content\": \"随着 AI Agent 从实验性工具加速进入生产系统，一个新的基础设施问题逐渐显露：当下主流的搜索工具，几乎都是为“人”设计的，而非为“AI”服务。 近日，一款AI搜索产品AnySearch正式发布，并在海外AI开发者圈引发关注。该产品专为AI Agent、企业AI系统设计，旨在为AI Agent提供统一、高质量、结构化的信息搜索层能力。 ...\", \"is_policy\": 0, \"origin_msg\": {\"id\": \"https://www.oschina.net/news/439927\", \"link\": \"https://www.oschina.net/news/439927\", \"tags\": [{\"term\": \"综合新闻\", \"label\": null, \"scheme\": null}], \"links\": [{\"rel\": \"alternate\", \"href\": \"https://www.oschina.net/news/439927\", \"type\": \"text/html\"}], \"title\": \"AnySearch 正式发布：为 AI Agent 构建的下一代搜索基础设施，重构搜索底层逻辑\", \"summary\": \"随着 AI Agent 从实验性工具加速进入生产系统，一个新的基础设施问题逐渐显露：当下主流的搜索工具，几乎都是为“人”设计的，而非为“AI”服务。 近日，一款AI搜索产品AnySearch正式发布，并在海外AI开发者圈引发关注。该产品专为AI Agent、企业AI系统设计，旨在为AI Agent提供统一、高质量、结构化的信息搜索层能力。 ...\", \"published\": \"Wed, 13 May 2026 10:33:23 +0800\", \"guidislink\": false, \"title_detail\": {\"base\": \"https://www.oschina.net/news/rss\", \"type\": \"text/plain\", \"value\": \"AnySearch 正式发布：为 AI Agent 构建的下一代搜索基础设施，重构搜索底层逻辑\", \"language\": n